+# Observer entry and cross-process clock: limited diagnostic — 2026-10-24
+
+Issue #112; #113 endurance and original M0 #20 remain open. This work changes Python
+diagnostic scripts only. No Cargo/Rust build, Rust executable invocation, Model launch,
+target native query, long pressure test or frozen-load/acceptance change occurred.
+
+## Failure preserved and repair
+
+The 495 failure remains a real failed native-diagnostic entry attempt: phase observer
+`importlib.util` was unavailable and the socket peer closed, before native region capture.
+Both observers now explicitly import that submodule. Their `--clock-handshake-only` mode
+exits before importing native support, reading target events or querying a target. Argument,
+path and executable hash checks still run; region starts its own tracemalloc.
+
+The original advisor found a second issue in the private v1 helper: its final receipt could
+replace previously exchanged timestamps with zeros while retaining locally ordered triples.
+The coordinator reproduced this using a controlled Python peer; the accepted invalid v1
+receipt and complete original scripts are retained, not relabelled as a successful handshake.
+
+Protocol v2 now binds the first five receipt timestamps to the actual exchange and checks:
+
+`parent_before <= child_sample <= parent_after <= child_before <= parent_sample <= child_after <= parent_receive`.
+
+The final ACK carries parent receive time; the child checks its order and receipt digest.
+PID/component, nonce, message stage, identity stability, explicit clock identity, three-second
+deadline and line cap remain. Both observer helper pins were updated together to
+`9c092e487ea1348901d70e6417f67096596f6f36c1f6405ea3eeb62a9d2f88ac`.
+Old v1 receipts are historical and do not establish v2 acceptance.
+
+## Actual bounded validation
+
+Evidence root: `/Volumes/HP P900/dev/MyCity/work/m0-observer-entry-clock-20261024/`.
+`fixed-observer-v2.zip` and `fixed-inputs.json` preserve seven exact script/document inputs;
+commands, logs, receipts and negative outputs are complete originals. All inputs were
+unchanged during execution. Post-run documentation is distinct from the frozen archive.
+
+- `01-clock-protocol`: 4 tests passed, including 14 malformed-parent-side branches, actual
+  helper subprocess receipt equality, wrong OS-parent PID and altered final ACK rejection.
+  Cases cover wrong clock name/ID/unit, component/PID, nonce/stage/echo, substituted receipt,
+  reversed cross-round order, future child time, EOF, excessive line and no-reply timeout.
+- `02-synthetic-boundaries`: original 14 tests passed; these use fake native/region data and
+  some real controlled Python clock exchanges, not a native target capture.
+- Both actual observer main entries launched with Python 3.9.6 `-B -I -S`, exit 0. The parent
+  and child receipts match exactly, including digest, actual Popen PID and interpreter path.
+  Both sides use `time.clock_gettime_ns(CLOCK_MONOTONIC)`, ID 6, nanoseconds, with the complete
