+# Candidate03 rare-batch control
+
+This directory contains a source-identity and refusal-control starter for candidate03's native observer run. It does not build, modify Rust source, create another observer, or make a performance acceptance claim. The prior `m0-t13a-rare` runner is historical evidence for an older candidate and is not reused as this candidate's identity.
+
+`source.schema.json` is the strict receipt contract. `source.json` is deliberately absent until the actual candidate's frozen extracted source tree, source archive, complete per-file manifest, `Cargo.lock`, binary, embedded fingerprint, successful build receipt, anchors, acceptance file, and policy file are frozen and hash-verified. Candidate03 is a frozen extracted source tree, not a Git checkout. Its fingerprint follows `crates/city-headless/build.rs`: sorted build-scope file names, each encoded as little-endian `u64` name length, UTF-8 name, little-endian `u64` content length, and original bytes. The scope is `.cargo/config.toml`, the other three root build inputs (`Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `rust-toolchain.toml`), and every file under `crates/` and `fixtures/`. The archive and manifest must live outside the extracted tree; extra files in that tree are rejected.
+
+The source contract binds the known 32c baseline archive and its business fixture hashes, then requires candidate/base file differences to equal an explicit frozen allowlist. Those baseline values are comparison inputs only; they do not identify candidate03's source, binary, workload, or result. No candidate path or digest is guessed.
+
+The source-derived report contract is now `source_derived_component_checks_not_executed`. `report_contract.py` checks actual model report fields: identity, complete trial count, cold-restore status, independent sample counts and conservative latency histograms. Source class 6 and class 7 must both qualify; each count population must equal its histogram population, and quantile ranks must match the actual sample count. Smoke has one trial and never meets the formal 200-trial gate. `observer_contract.py` separately checks the exact native command/source/binary identity, exit/cleanup, reported coverage holes and unchanged guard arithmetic. Neither summary checker proves raw identity coverage, actual snapshot overlap, physical memory or full M0. The Rust report's formal status remains `not_evaluated_pending_original_latency_and_observer_audit`.
+
+`--inspect claims|source smoke|formal` is read-only and selects the fixed corresponding `rb3-*-01/observed` directory. It first verifies the pinned source/build inputs, then prints independent model/observer component results and report hashes. It does not launch a model, produce an acceptance receipt or replace independent raw evidence review. Missing source identity or reports is a refusal. Its exit code is an inspection result, never the complete performance gate. The launch path is implemented but currently refuses because the real frozen candidate/build receipt and executed helper regression receipt are absent. `--test-helpers` is an explicit future action: it first refuses active compiler/model jobs, runs the actual helper suite once in a fresh evidence directory, and retains stdout/stderr and exact helper hashes. `--run` requires that successful unchanged receipt before source loading or model creation.
+No arguments or `--plan` only prints the preparation state; neither creates measurement files. The source-only run gate is designed to verify the pinned identities, external `work` and shared `target` links, SSD profile/free space, live process state, and 120 seconds of normal pressure within the frozen swap cap. It must refuse MyCity measurement/native-observer processes and Cargo/Rust compiler or documentation builds. Process refusals may record only PID, executable basename, and reason. The process inventory uses `ps -axo pid=,ppid=,comm=` and preserves spaces in the complete executable path; an active headless process without reliable arguments is refused rather than guessed idle. Each process check must be repeated before every command and source identity checked again after it.
+
+The source receipt pins unchanged world, raw-metric, per-trial raw, combined-log, swap-growth, pressure, and free-space caps. Source and cell samples share the actual worker raw file; there is no invented independent class-7 raw quota. The histogram has 40,001 u32 buckets (160,004 bytes minimum per nonempty collector), following the existing conservative 1us histogram. This is a minimum backing estimate, not a new arena allowance or proof of measured allocation capacity. The original role/common budgets remain unchanged. It must use short work names (`rb3-cs-01`, `rb3-cf-01`, `rb3-ss-01`, `rb3-sf-01`) and validate the resolved external socket path `observed/model/normal-pool/pool.sock` before creating a run directory. The encoded pathname including NUL must be below macOS `sun_path` capacity.
+
+A formal stratum requires a successful, freshly reclassified smoke execution receipt for the same stratum, source fingerprint, and binary digest. The native invocation is:
+
+```text
+SAME_EXE native-observe OBS_ROOT -- SAME_EXE scale-rare-batch ANCHORS OBS_ROOT/model claims|source smoke|formal
+```
+
+The wrapper must clear inherited `MYCITY_*` and `RUST_MIN_STACK` variables but must not set any `MYCITY_*` variables itself. The native watcher owns process registration, nonce, heap log, and observer clock. The launch path preserves command output, raw observer/model artifacts, frozen inputs, per-command wall time, and failures in a new non-overwriting work directory. They do not retry or clean results.
+
+The eventual result must distinguish collection completion, actual count, selected latency, observer caps, class-6 values, and both class-7 gates. This wrapper does not establish the wider rare-class matrix; the remaining compute classes still need their own evidence; the frozen acceptance fixture enumerates ten classes in total. Full M0 and the real 16 GB device gate remain `not_run`.
+
+This preparation is source-only and `not_run`. Helper regression cases are present but have not been executed. No model run, observer run, build, benchmark, storage cleanup, or new target was performed. The candidate source receipt is missing; component classifiers and their synthetic regression cases have only been AST parsed. The admission implementation and launch path are untested; independent raw evidence review remains incomplete. No candidate03 measurement has been launched. Measured executables must live in preserved external work, outside the mutable shared target. After admission, source/support hashes, process and storage guards, pressure and swap are checked again; stale admission is rejected. Original failures are not overwritten or automatically retried.
+
+No helper, admission or launch command was executed during the live eight-hour measurement. The launch code does not create another Python measurement observer and does not inject any MYCITY variables. A zero inspection/execution exit indicates only sufficient reported components; raw/cadence/identity/overlap review and physical memory remain separate gates.
+
+The controller serializes `--test-helpers` and `--run` using a nonblocking repository lock. Model liveness checks remain mandatory; the lock alone is not proof that the host is idle.
+
+Offline numeric checking is implemented in `duration_audit.py` and `batch_audit.py`. `--audit claims|source smoke|formal` first refuses live compiler/model jobs, verifies source/helper identities and a complete terminal native collection, then reads the exact `eligible_duration_ranges` emitted by the analysis child. Whole-file SHA, aligned nonoverlapping 9-byte ranges, per-file and total sample counts, exact global nearest-rank quantiles and Rust conservative histogram intervals are crosschecked. It never averages per-file quantiles. Fewer than 200 records cannot pass the numeric latency gate, even if all records are fast. The original 20ms/40ms limits are unchanged.
+
+This offline action runs after the native observer exits, using a separate QA memory scope. Its worst-case Python scratch estimate is about 420 MiB at the capped 600 files, not a claim that analysis fits the 1 MiB game DRIVER. The 600-file bound derives from 200 trials with at most three producers each; source normally selects at most two worker files per trial. Range eligibility is still asserted by the Rust analysis and requires separate transaction/process/pool/snapshot audit. A matching numeric report does not prove 200 independent trials, physical-memory acceptance, or full M0. The offline action preserves its input hashes and writes a fresh report without changing any original raw files. It has not been executed.
